Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

0.3.0 is unusable from PyPI: the wheel carries no
`store/migrations/*.sql`, so the first call fails with
`no such table: policies`. The fix landed in the repo but a repo fix
helps nobody until it is released.

Verified rather than assumed: built the wheel, installed it into a clean
3.12 virtualenv outside the source tree, and ran migrations. All three
migrations apply and both `policies` and `policy_versions` exist. That is
the exact path that fails on 0.3.0.

README test count corrected, 63 -> 111.

0.3.0 should be yanked once this is up, so pip stops resolving to a
release that cannot start.
---
 README.md      | 2 +-
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index bb30c21..9fc32e7 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ Requires Python ≥ 3.12.
 
 ```bash
 pip install -e ".[dev]"
-pytest                    # 63 tests — the guardrail suite is the release blocker
+pytest                    # 111 tests — the guardrail suite is the release blocker
 python -m scripts.demo    # one of everything, end to end, zero external deps
 ```
 
diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index ed84700..d61ecfa 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 [project]
 name = "onedoor"
-version = "0.3.0"
+version = "0.3.1"
 description = "A tiered guardrail/policy engine for agentic systems: default-deny, bounds, caps, approvals, dry-run, kill switch, and reversibility as a precondition for autonomy."
 readme = "README.md"
 requires-python = ">=3.12"
